WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.208 --> 00:00:04.375
It's hard work, working with people like Anya
and Mimî, because they are just

00:00:04.375 --> 00:00:06.375
constantly trying to fuck me up.

00:00:11.458 --> 00:00:13.958
I love to laugh on set, 
and I love to have fun, and-

00:00:14.625 --> 00:00:19.916
the good thing is that Henry is also 
like that. And he’s very good at it, 

00:00:19.916 --> 00:00:24.333
I don’t know if he’s a stand up comedian 
or what you know, it’s like...

00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:25.958
he’s a very funny guy!

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:28.916
Henry will turn around and say
some shit, and you’re 

00:00:28.916 --> 00:00:31.333
just like, arhhh…

00:00:31.333 --> 00:00:32.750
we're just about to do this thing.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:34.916
Why you got to throw us off like that?!

00:00:34.916 --> 00:00:36.416
And he will just come out with these one liners,

00:00:36.416 --> 00:00:39.375
he's like the king
of, like, these dry one liners,

00:00:39.375 --> 00:00:41.250
and they just
have you in tears of laughter.

00:00:41.375 --> 00:00:44.708
At your final breath, a shitless death. 

00:00:46.541 --> 00:00:47.625
But I doubt it. 

00:00:49.375 --> 00:00:51.416
Eamon gets up to some shenanigans. 

00:00:52.791 --> 00:00:57.000
So if I’m with Eamon, who plays Cahir, we’ll probably laugh the whole way through 

00:00:57.375 --> 00:01:01.125
because he is just the ultimate joker,
and he's a tease as well

00:01:01.541 --> 00:01:03.166
and I'm very guillble. So that's-

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.250
that’s a really funny combination.

00:01:06.583 --> 00:01:13.083
Ahh we’ve all got an inner joker. I’d say
Eamon is the joker. 

00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:15.375
He loves it, he loves making people laugh. 

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.291
Shut up. 

00:01:18.666 --> 00:01:19.750
He's hilarious.

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:22.250
He's just on fire all the time on set.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:23.458
He's just so funny.

00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:25.708
Anya and Mimî are just ridiculous,

00:01:25.708 --> 00:01:29.083
and they always try to distract me on set,
but I am a constant professional.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:32.875
I'm the serious one.

00:01:35.208 --> 00:01:38.541
We were walking, I don’t know what we were doing there to be honest, 

00:01:38.541 --> 00:01:39.166
but we were walking,

00:01:39.166 --> 00:01:43.291
and there was these like boulders
everywhere you went, so you couldn't walk.

00:01:43.291 --> 00:01:46.708
And the director at the time, Sarah, she was like “What’s wrong with you guys?” 

00:01:46.708 --> 00:01:47.625
“Can you not just walk?”

00:01:47.625 --> 00:01:50.666
And we were like struggling
because our ankles were just getting

00:01:50.666 --> 00:01:51.625
destroyed.

00:01:52.666 --> 00:01:54.041
Afraid to break a nail princess?

00:01:54.041 --> 00:01:59.041
I'm from the north of England originally,
and being back in the north of England,

00:02:00.166 --> 00:02:01.250
Jaskier...

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:04.750
was for the first few takes, really-

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:08.250
Geordie and I had turned to Henry
and I was like “Do I sound a bit Geordie?”

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.875
And he was like,
“Yeah, you sound weird, man.”

00:02:10.875 --> 00:02:12.875
You need a nap!

00:02:12.875 --> 00:02:14.083
A lot of our views

00:02:14.083 --> 00:02:16.333
and perspectives
have all been green screened.

00:02:17.333 --> 00:02:21.625
So me and Eamon will show each other little
video clips of what we're imagining.

00:02:21.791 --> 00:02:25.250
So it'd be like, “Oh, I'm imagining
Kanye West singing Happy Birthday

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:26.333
to Dave Chappelle.”

00:02:28.583 --> 00:02:30.583
Yas is pretty bad

00:02:31.125 --> 00:02:33.416
because he would always come up
with different nicknames.

00:02:34.083 --> 00:02:35.750
He started calling me Lambchop.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:37.416
Good old Lambchop!

00:02:37.416 --> 00:02:40.041
They just kept it in because they
they liked it.

00:02:40.041 --> 00:02:41.291
Just a bit of fun.

00:02:41.291 --> 00:02:44.875
Henry and I have a small game
where usually

00:02:44.875 --> 00:02:47.916
if one of us leaves a take
and we're still in the scene

00:02:49.041 --> 00:02:51.666
we try and pull faces
at each other to try and make each other

00:02:51.666 --> 00:02:52.166
laugh.

00:02:52.166 --> 00:02:55.375
He's got a really good number of just leaving a take, like looking really serious

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:56.541
like Geralt,

00:02:56.541 --> 00:02:57.833
and then just as he,

00:02:57.833 --> 00:02:59.625
leaves frame, he'll just go-

00:03:01.333 --> 00:03:05.250
Me and Paul are on set...
there's always something going on, always,

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:08.541
there's always some sort of trick or prank
that everyone's playing, especially

00:03:08.541 --> 00:03:12.208
with Freya as well,
because she's so competitive.

00:03:12.208 --> 00:03:14.625
Maybe, I might even let you win.

00:03:14.625 --> 00:03:16.458
Pfft, yeah, you wish.

00:03:16.458 --> 00:03:18.750
There was one scene
that we were filming recently,

00:03:19.083 --> 00:03:22.416
and I think it's
when Cahir enters Cintra.

00:03:22.416 --> 00:03:25.166
At the end, there’s like this face off
between the three of us.

00:03:25.583 --> 00:03:29.166
And like the cameras just kept on rolling
and it felt like an eternity.

00:03:43.208 --> 00:03:45.208
We were all in character,
just staring at each other.

00:03:45.208 --> 00:03:48.083
But Eamon was on the other side
of the camera, so he's just staring at us.

00:03:48.083 --> 00:03:48.583
And then he's like,

00:03:49.916 --> 00:03:52.250
like that, and he’s just doing loads
of funny things,

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:54.041
he's just brilliant.

00:03:54.041 --> 00:03:57.958
Look, it's hard work
working with people like Anya and Mimî

00:03:57.958 --> 00:04:01.208
because they are just constantly
trying to fuck me up.

00:04:01.208 --> 00:04:01.500
Sorry.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:05.458
Excuse my language, but,
you know, Anya is constantly yelling at me

00:04:05.458 --> 00:04:06.958
trying to get her tea for her.

00:04:08.083 --> 00:04:10.833
 It seems mages are merciful. 

00:04:11.458 --> 00:04:15.375
Mimî is like, you know, making faces off
camera so I don't get my close up

00:04:15.375 --> 00:04:16.750
right. Like, it's a nightmare dude.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:18.208
Like...it's a nightmare.

00:04:19.875 --> 00:04:23.375
I do find it really funny, though,
because obviously we're not actually fighting

00:04:23.375 --> 00:04:28.791
these monsters, they’re you know,
big puppets, or stunt men

00:04:28.791 --> 00:04:33.250
in blue suits! So sometimes you find yourself laughing a little bit. 

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.625
So the first time we saw them come in,
it was like these two guys, like

00:04:36.958 --> 00:04:39.750
in these blue rubber suits. And me and Paul-

00:04:40.916 --> 00:04:41.541
I looked at Paul

00:04:41.541 --> 00:04:43.041
I was like, “Who let the condoms out man?”

00:04:45.125 --> 00:04:45.833
It's so funny.

00:04:45.833 --> 00:04:49.666
Big foam heads with, like,
stunt men in blue spandex.

00:04:50.625 --> 00:04:52.000
It's so good.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:52.958
It's so good.

00:04:55.416 --> 00:04:59.541
Aqueducts because... it was testing conditions

00:04:59.541 --> 00:05:02.041
because we had to be in the water,
visualize this monster.

00:05:02.041 --> 00:05:03.458
But we had so much fun.

00:05:05.375 --> 00:05:07.208
That was one of my favorite scenes
to film,

00:05:07.208 --> 00:05:07.750
for sure.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:10.708
Training Ciri in Episode 3.

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:12.916
Freya, you know, kind of challenging

00:05:12.916 --> 00:05:16.750
Lambert and testing his authority.

00:05:17.166 --> 00:05:18.125
What did you do then?

00:05:18.416 --> 00:05:20.916
And then taking control of the situation.

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:27.500
Cahir and Yennefer are sort of in the middle of this square.

00:05:27.583 --> 00:05:30.041
And they arrive, sort of above ground
and they sort of

00:05:30.041 --> 00:05:32.750
have it out together and they share,
I think,

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:38.000
I mean, you know, Cahir and Yennefer
are pretty closed off people,

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.416
I think they're pretty protected people,

00:05:39.416 --> 00:05:42.916
and so for the first time, I think
because they're strangers, they kind of

00:05:43.333 --> 00:05:47.125
are the most emotionally available
that they've ever been with anyone.

00:05:47.666 --> 00:05:54.875
Everyone answers to someone eventually. Even you I suspect. 

00:05:56.166 --> 00:05:57.833
Fringilla...

00:05:57.833 --> 00:06:02.291
she finally gets to have a bit,
just a little bit of revenge.

00:06:02.291 --> 00:06:04.333
And we've also got this
character called Hake.

00:06:04.333 --> 00:06:07.333
He's a general,
and he is winding her up, galore.

00:06:07.375 --> 00:06:09.958
Like everything that she does, he's
nit picky on it.

00:06:11.333 --> 00:06:13.791
He keeps throwing her
under the bus in front of Cahir.

00:06:13.791 --> 00:06:15.875
And you call yourself a leader…

00:06:18.541 --> 00:06:21.750
She’s just had enough, so she gets to come in

00:06:22.416 --> 00:06:24.333
and basically kill all the generals.

00:06:24.708 --> 00:06:31.625
Whenever a lesser light tries to steal what is yours you do not sit there and take it. 

00:06:33.458 --> 00:06:36.416
It's amazing.
It’s such a fierce moment.

00:06:36.625 --> 00:06:39.583
My first scene I think that I shot was

00:06:39.583 --> 00:06:42.583
me and the big man, farting about by a lake.

00:06:42.583 --> 00:06:44.958
It was the first time I'd seen HC for-

00:06:45.833 --> 00:06:48.208
for a year over the pandemic.

00:06:48.208 --> 00:06:52.875
So it felt really like coming home
and it was so easy to slip back in.

00:06:52.875 --> 00:06:56.000
Each of your faces is cause enough for celebration.

00:06:57.875 --> 00:07:01.375
 You’re safe, you made it back, you made it home. 

